--- body ---
## Context

`erg validate` with no arguments defaults to `tickets/`, and
`loadErgs` walks that tree recursively. As the `tickets/` directory
grows subdirs (`closed/`, `archive/`, `integration/`), the recursive
walk creates problems:

- Duplicate-ID errors when an archived ticket shares an ID with a
  top-level ticket (observed: `0024` existed in both `tickets/` and
  `tickets/archive/` — fixed by removing the stray copy, but the
  validator shouldn't depend on manual hygiene to avoid false alarms).
- Validating `closed/` and `archive/` on every run is wasteful when
  only active tickets change.

## Actions

1. Change `cmdValidate` default from `tickets/` to non-recursive
   (only direct `.erg` children of `tickets/`).
2. Explicit subdir paths still work: `erg validate tickets/closed/`
   validates closed tickets on demand.
3. Update `test_validate.sh`: the `real tickets pass` test should
   pass with the new default without needing to exclude subdirs.
4. Document the new default in `README.md` (one line under `validate`).

## Follow-on (separate ticket if warranted)

- `erg validate --changed`: derive the ticket list from
  `git diff --name-only HEAD` for fast CI incremental runs.

## Exit criteria

- `erg validate` (no args) only scans top-level `tickets/*.erg`.
- `erg validate tickets/closed/` still works.
- `make test` passes including `real tickets pass`.
- `erg validate` help/usage reflects the new default.
